# Testing Rules

## Running Tests
```bash
# Unit tests
npm test

# Type checking
npx tsc --noEmit

# Linting
npm run lint

# Build check
npm run build

# E2E tests (requires dev server)
npx playwright test

# All checks before PR
npm test && npm run lint && npm run build
```

## Unit Tests
- Location: `tests/*.test.mjs`
- Tool: Node.js built-in test runner (`node:test`)
- Test pure functions and utilities only
- Do NOT test UI rendering in unit tests (use Playwright)

## E2E Tests (Playwright)
- Location: `tests/e2e/`
- Test critical user journeys end-to-end
- Required flows:
  1. Auth (signup, login, logout)
  2. Job browsing and applying
  3. Application tracking
  4. Profile management

## Test Philosophy
- Unit tests for pure logic (utils, calculations, validators)
- E2E tests for user journeys (auth, CRUD flows)
- No UI component tests (Playwright covers this)

## What to Test
Always add tests when:
- Writing a new utility function
- Adding a new auth flow
- Adding a form mutation
- Fixing a bug (regression test)

## Test Naming
```javascript
// Clear intent:
test('calculateLevel returns 1 for 0 XP', () => {...})
test('formatCurrency formats USD correctly', () => {...})
test('isEmpty returns true for empty strings', () => {...})

// NOT:
test('calculateLevel works', () => {...})
```

## Before Committing
1. `npm test` — all unit tests pass
2. `npx tsc --noEmit` — no type errors
3. `npm run lint` — no lint errors
4. `npm run build` — production build succeeds
